  "lawGrade": "MAPPED",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Yukawa potential V(r) = -g^2 e^(-mr)/r: short-range, enormously strong at close range, with confinement structure. The mapping: strongest force <-> greatest commandment; short range <-> love requires proximity and presence; confinement <-> covenant permanence; asymptotic freedom <-> in deep intimacy love does not crush. Fruits of the Spirit two-tier ruling (v4, AM-3): Tier 1 (Love, Peace, Joy) DERIVED as stationary eigenmodes of the Yukawa potential at equilibrium; Tier 2 (Patience, Kindness, Goodness, Faithfulness, Gentleness, Self-control) are structural correspondences, not derived, and are excluded from the theorem count. Retired: all nine fruits from one unified Hamiltonian.",
  "statementPlain": "The strongest force in nature binds at close range and, paradoxically, loosens its grip at the closest range - deep intimacy does not crush. The proposed reading: that is the shape of covenant love. On canon rulings, three fruits (love, peace, joy) are derived from the potential's stationary structure; the other six remain correspondences, not derivations - the stronger claim was tried, abandoned, and is formally retired. The physics is established; the love mapping is proposed, not proven beyond the Tier-1 stationary calculation, whose receipt is external to this repo.",
  "mathematicalForm": "V(r) = -g^2 e^(-mr)/r; Tier 1: stationary eigenmodes of V at equilibrium -> {Love, Peace, Joy}",
  "mathFormNormal": "V(r) = -g^2 e^(-mr)/r; Tier 1: stationary eigenmodes of V at equilibrium -> {Love, Peace, Joy}",
